00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.760
So Dataprep is developed
by Trifacta in partnership

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.230
with Google Cloud.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:02.620
Trifacta as a company
and as a product

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.040
is the recognized leader
in data preparation.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.740
Trifacta also offers
solutions that

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:11.480
run on over Cloud platforms.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:16.840
It runs also on its own
Trifacta SaaS, or on-premise.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.570
So you can really select the
version of the product that

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.620
fits your needs.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:24.410
Cloud Dataprep on
the Google Cloud

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:28.060
is the serverless and only
native to the Google Cloud Data

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.740
Preparation solution as part of
the broader Google Cloud Smart

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.900
Analytic suites.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.800
Cloud Dataprep allows data
analysts, business analysts,

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.880
and engineers and
data scientists

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.900
to explore clean and
prepared big data visual.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.570
As you can see on the
left of the screen,

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.850
Cloud Dataprep
connects to BigQuery,

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.400
Cloud storage, Google
Sheets, as well as

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.400
traditional databases
and Cloud apps.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.810
At the center, you can
see that Cloud Dataprep

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:59.890
is built on top of Dataflow.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:05.110
What it means is that any data
transformation containing rules

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.940
that design in Cloud Dataprep
is pushed down to Dataflow

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.950
and can easily
scale to transform

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.530
any data, big or small.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:17.350
Now focusing on the right
part of the diagram,

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:20.360
once your data is ready in
BigQuery or Cloud storage,

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.670
you can analyze it with Google
Cloud Data Studio or Looker.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.790
You can try enmeshing learning
models with Google Cloud ML

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.460
Services, or you
can even get insight

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:34.210
from over a partner
VI Solutions,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.880
such as Qlik or Tableau.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:41.020
Now if we just focus on
the bottom of the screen,

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:46.810
Cloud Dataprep is a native
services to Google Cloud.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:52.220
It provides APIs that we can
leverage with other technology,

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.930
or Google technologies such
as Cloud Composer, [INAUDIBLE]

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.320
APIs to schedule and to
orchestrate Cloud Dataprep,

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.060
or leverage Cloud functions.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:06.130
For example, when a file
arrives in Google Cloud Storage,

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:09.920
you can trigger a
Cloud Dataprep flow.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.340
So this is a summary of an
overview of Cloud Dataprep

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:16.960
and where it fits
in the Google Cloud.

